# Cloudflare Pages redirects — old 8-page site to the new build.
# NOT DEPLOYED. Rationale, evidence and honesty notes: 06-launch/REDIRECT_MAP.md
# Copy into 05-build/site/ at deploy time (Gate F), not before.
#
# /path and /builder are NOT listed here. Both carried query-parameter deep links
# (?p=<role>, ?path=<role>, ?b=<stack>) and Cloudflare Pages does not reliably match on
# query strings, so both are handled by real pages in the build that read the parameter
# and route correctly. A blanket redirect would have silently collapsed 15 deep links.
#
# The old .html forms (/explorer.html etc.) already 307 to their clean URLs on the
# current host, so they chain into the rules below and need no separate entries.

# --- strong mappings: the new page does the same job
/pathways   /f/ai-ml/      301
/learn      /method/       301
/explorer   /x/            301
/nocred     /x/?c=absence  301

# --- weak mapping: best approximation, 302 on purpose
/patterns   /method/       302

# No blanket redirect to / — mass-redirecting to a homepage is a soft-404
# pattern that strands the reader and is discounted by search engines.
